      "created_at_shanghai": "2026-11-04 00:07:23",
      "type": "引用",
      "type_label": "引用",
      "text": "And electrical equipment, cooling, networking and batteries",
      "quote": {
        "author": "euwyn",
        "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2033571359117426688/MZRPvEvM_200x200.jpg",
        "created_at_shanghai": "2026-11-03 19:00:19",
        "created_at_utc": "2026-11-03T11:00:19.000Z",
        "id": "2117572576390349155",
        "images": [
          "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2117572503589818368/img/W1ePJqajOzRNpz9x.jpg"
        ],
        "media": [
          {
            "duration": 68.651,
            "height": 1080,
            "thumbnail_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2117572503589818368/img/W1ePJqajOzRNpz9x.jpg",
            "type": "video",
            "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2117572503589818368/vid/avc1/1920x1080/Ku78wKr8uh9nnmN9.mp4?tag=16",
            "width": 1920
          }
        ],
        "name": "Euwyn",
        "text": "Elon Musk says the AI boom will hit a WALL by the end of 2026.\n\nHe says the whole industry is about to learn a hard lesson in hardware.\n\nChip output is exploding, but electricity is nearly flat everywhere outside China.\n\nSo the two lines cross this year.\n\nHe says by the end of the year, we will be making more AI chips than we can actually turn on.\n\nMillions of them pile up with nowhere to plug in.\n\nIn his words, the bottleneck for the next year is not chips, it is raw power.\n\nWhoever can turn on the most chips fastest wins the race.\n\nIn the end, the AI race comes down to one thing:\n\nRaw electricity.\n\n— Elon Musk (.@elonmusk) on Dwarkesh Patel's (.@dwarkesh_sp) podcast",
        "url": "https://x.com/euwyn/status/2117572576390349155",
        "verified": true,
        "verified_type": "individual"
      },
